! C2H8O3 | Unconstrained optimization of forward-IRC endpoint
! wB97X-D/6-21G+(d,p)/PCM(water) -- same level throughout the aa001
! series, so this optimization is fully consistent with the IRC search
! itself (no level-of-theory mismatch, unlike the earlier chloroacetaldehyde
! work where the IRC and the refinement level differed).
!
! Starting geometry: the final point reached by the forward IRC run
! (aa001e.log), i.e. one endpoint of the reaction path. Constraints
! removed entirely -- this is a genuine, unconstrained RUNTYP=OPTIMIZE to
! let this endpoint fully relax to its nearest true minimum.
!
! No $HESS input needed: RUNTYP=OPTIMIZE defaults to HESS=GUESS
! regardless of coordinate system (Cartesian or internal/DLC) -- this
! default already worked cleanly for aa001a/aa001b/aa001c. HSSEND=.t. and
! $FORCE PURIFY=.t. retained to get a clean final frequency analysis,
! confirming genuine minimum status (should show zero imaginary
! frequencies, all six trans/rot modes at 0.00 given PURIFY is correctly
! placed in $FORCE this time).

 $BASIS GBASIS=N21 NGAUSS=6 NDFUNC=1 NPFUNC=1 DIFFSP=.t. $END
 $CONTRL SCFTYP=RHF RUNTYP=OPTIMIZE NZVAR=33 $END
 $CONTRL DFTTYP=wB97X-D $END
 $SCF DIIS=.t. DAMP=.t. $END
 $STATPT OPTTOL=0.00005 NSTEP=200 IHREP=20 HSSEND=.t. $END
 $ZMAT DLC=.t. AUTO=.t. $END
 $ZMAT NONVDW(1)=8,13, 10,7, 7,3, 8,10 $END
 $FORCE METHOD=SEMINUM PURIFY=.t. $END
 $PCM SOLVNT=WATER $END
 $SYSTEM MWORDS=25 MEMDDI=24 $END
!$CONTRL EXETYP=CHECK $END

 $DATA
Acetaldehyde hydrate and water -- forward IRC endpoint, unconstrained opt
C1
H     1.0   3.1699626804   0.6353905231  -0.2505676751
C     6.0   2.9242219615   0.1716395096  -1.2092523877
